  "segment": "bootstrap-config",
  "source_text": "Arbiter uses Hydra to compose one validated runtime config from YAML files in the conf directory. For this demo, we create one mail-demo account for SMTP and IMAP. Bootstrap the server config. Then bootstrap the SMTP account and policy. Edit the generated SMTP files for the local test server. Activate the SMTP account and show the composed config. Bootstrap .arbiter.env, inspect the generated variables, and enter the SMTP credentials. Add the matching IMAP account. Edit it for the local test server. Activate IMAP, then run env bootstrap again; it adds IMAP variables without losing the SMTP values. Enter the IMAP credentials. Now run a normal config check. Finally, run a live config check; while it runs, Arbiter logs into the test IMAP and SMTP servers.",
